                        "glosses": [
                            "To swell; to puff."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "26bdd9bf-cea1-4065-8110-1fc99cf60640",
                                "sense_id": "0727b839-2649-32a1-893f-503fa0fb26dd",
                                "text": "and when the great raines or water cometh and ſinketh thorow the gravell, and cometh to the earth, then the earth ſwelleth and bolneth, and waxeth ſoft, and with treading, and eſpecially with carriage, the gravel ſinketh and goeth downwards; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b7d76f4-be22-4fff-b8dc-f832e34a89e1",
                                "sense_id": "0727b839-2649-32a1-893f-503fa0fb26dd",
                                "text": "Se howe this toode bolneth:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "548b31fd-f842-46db-8a7d-97a58439f3a5",
                                "sense_id": "0727b839-2649-32a1-893f-503fa0fb26dd",
                                "text": "For it is better to Sleepe lyttle and somewhat wyth watching to soke away humous, then immoderatly to bolne, swell and therewyth throughly to be cloyed."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
